                <pb facs="0660" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/106a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-12T20:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1746. This Government has purchased approximately 6300 tons of tungsten and 6700
                    tons of antimony from the Chinese Government, for shipment from Haiphong and
                    Saigon, Indochina, where it has been in storage. The United States vessels, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Puerto Rican</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Birmingham
                        City</hi>, of the Isthmian Line, will carry these cargoes to the United
                    States; the <hi rendition="#italic">Puerto Rican</hi> is now loading and the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Birmingham City</hi> will load during the latter part of
                    the month. Please place this information informally before the appropriate
                    British officials and request that British naval officers be instructed to
                    permit the free movement of these vessels.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
